+### 1. src/citesure/citations.py (D1 input formats)
+- Dataclass `Citation`: fields citation_id (str), url (str), claim (str),
+  source_text (str, optional raw context).
+- `extract_citations(text: str, url_map: dict[str,str] | None = None) -> list[Citation]`
+  handling BOTH markdown forms:
+  a) inline numeric markers `[1]`, `[2]` … resolved via url_map (e.g. a
+     "## Sources" section mapping "1" -> url, or an explicit dict);
+  b) inline link form `[source](url)` / `[label](https://...)` where the URL is
+     in the link itself.
+- Claim unit (D4): the sentence (or paragraph, if no sentence boundary) that
+  contains the marker is the claim text. Store it in `claim`.
+- `load_input(path: str) -> tuple[list[Citation], dict]`: reads a file and
+  auto-detects format:
+  - structured JSON: a list of {"claim": ..., "citation": url-or-id} objects
+    (also accept {"citations": [...]} wrapper);
+  - markdown: parse inline citations as above; also parse a trailing
+    "## Sources"/"## References" section (`[1]: url` reference-style links or
+    numbered list lines) into the url_map.
+  Return (citations, meta) where meta may carry e.g. {"format": "json"|"markdown"}.
+
+### 2. src/citesure/fetcher.py (D7 — follow exactly)
+- httpx-based async fetcher + trafilatura for HTML→clean text.
+- 5s timeout per request; 2 retries with exponential backoff (e.g. 0.5s, 1.5s).
+- Max 10 concurrent fetches (asyncio.Semaphore).
+- Custom User-Agent identifying citesure, e.g.
+  "citesure/0.1.0 (+https://github.com/DawnofGenX/citesure)".
+- Respect robots.txt (urllib.robotparser; fetch robots.txt once per domain,
+  cache it; disallowed → treat as unreachable with a note, do NOT fetch).
+- 24h disk cache keyed by URL+etag, stored under ~/.cache/citesure/
+  (make the cache dir overridable via env var CITECHECK_CACHE_DIR for tests).
+- Support file:// URLs AND bare local paths (read from disk, no network) —
+  required for offline tests/demos.
+- NO headless browser. JS-rendered pages are out of scope (D8).
+- Public API: `async def fetch(url: str) -> FetchedPage` where FetchedPage has
+  url, ok (bool), status_code (int|None), text (clean text via trafilatura,
+  fallback to raw text), html (raw), etag (str|None), error (str|None),
+  paywall_detected (bool), retraction_detected (bool), fetched_from_cache (bool).
+- Paywall detection: simple heuristics on HTML/text (login forms, "paywall",
+  "subscribe", "sign in to continue", metered-access markers). Retraction
