+# TASK: citesure Phase 2 — Overlap tier + reporting
+
+You are working inside an existing repo at /home/hermes/citesure/. Read PLAN.md
+in the repo root first — every "Locked Decision" (D1–D12) is binding. Do not
+deviate. Phase 1 (core engine) is already complete and committed: citations.py,
+fetcher.py, reachability.py, cli.py, models.py, tests/ all exist and pass.
+Read those files before writing anything — build ON TOP of them, do not rewrite.
+
+## What you must build (all under /home/hermes/citesure/)
+
+### 1. src/citesure/overlap.py (D4 matching engine — the heart of this phase)
+Citation-anchored windows, NO whole-page matching:
+- Claim unit = the sentence/paragraph containing the citation marker (already
+  extracted as `Citation.claim` in Phase 1).
+- Passage segmentation: split fetched page text into passages (sentences or
+  short paragraphs — your choice, document it).
+- Top-k passage selection: rank passages by relevance to the claim (e.g.
+  token/Jaccard overlap of content terms + entity-ish tokens like capitalized
+  words, numbers, quoted strings). k default ~5, configurable.
+- Overlap scoring: score = overlap between claim terms and the best-matching
+  passage(s). Design a deterministic, unit-testable scoring function
+  (e.g. weighted Jaccard / term-coverage ratio in [0,1]). NO LLM, NO embeddings
+  in this tier (NLI is Phase 3).
+- Verdict logic per D3:
+  - strong overlap (score >= high threshold, e.g. 0.6) → supported
+  - weak/partial overlap (mid band, e.g. 0.3–0.6) → ambiguous
+  - claim absent from cited region (score < low threshold, e.g. < 0.3) → unsupported
+  - page unreachable/paywalled → keep Phase-1 statuses (unreachable/paywalled)
+  - marker not locatable / JS page → ambiguous (per D3)
+  - Make thresholds module-level constants so tests can pin them.
+- User-supplied excerpts: if input provides an explicit excerpt for a citation
+  (JSON form may carry an "excerpt" field), match against THAT instead of the
+  fetched page (D4: "User-supplied excerpts accepted as input option").
+- Public API: `def score_overlap(claim: str, passages: list[str]) -> tuple[float, str]`
+  (returns best score + best passage snippet) and
+  `async def verify_citations(citations, *, use_overlap=True) -> Report`
+  (or extend the existing verify flow — integrate cleanly with Phase 1's
+  reachability tier: fetch → classify reachability → if reachable, run overlap
+  tier → final status; tier_reached=2 when overlap ran).
+
+### 2. Reporting (extend cli.py + new report module if you like)
+- All 5 statuses must be producible and correctly counted in Report (D3).
+- `--strict` flag: ambiguous counts as FAILURE (CI mode) — implement properly
+  now (Phase 1 accepted the flag; make it real: with --strict, exit code is 0
+  only if no unsupported AND no ambiguous AND pass_rate >= threshold; document
+  exact semantics in --help).
+- Output formats:
+  - default: human-readable Markdown-style report to stdout (per-citation lines
+    with status emoji/symbol, url, score, evidence snippet; summary block with
+    total/supported/unsupported/unverifiable/pass_rate);
+  - `--json`: full report.to_dict() JSON (already exists — keep working);
+  - `--md` optional: write markdown report to file (nice-to-have; implement if
+    quick, else note it).
+- Exit codes: 0 iff (pass_rate >= threshold) AND (not --strict OR no ambiguous)
+  else 1. Document in --help.
+
+### 3. Fixtures — complete the D9 corpus (tests/fixtures/)
