+# TASK: citesure Phase 3 — NLI tier (DeBERTa-v3 cross-encoder)
+
+You are working inside an existing repo at /home/hermes/citesure/. Read PLAN.md
+in the repo root first — every "Locked Decision" (D1–D12) is binding. Do not
+deviate. Phases 1–2 are complete and committed: citations.py, fetcher.py,
+reachability.py, overlap.py, cli.py, models.py, tests/ all exist and pass.
+Read those files before writing anything — build ON TOP of them.
+
+## Locked decisions relevant to you (verbatim from PLAN.md)
+- D2: "NLI entailment — local cross-encoder scores entailment. Tiers 1+2 are
+  the default path; tier 3 is a first-class opt-in (--nli), fully built and
+  tested, NOT a stub"
+- D3: verdict model; "unsupported = page fetched but claim absent from cited
+  region AND (NLI < 0.3 when on); ambiguous = partial overlap, NLI 0.3–0.7
+  band, or marker not locatable (JS page)"
+- D6: "NLI model: cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base default (~425 MB), lazy
+  download on first --nli use, cached to ~/.cache/citesure/. Model swap at 3
+  levels (priority order): --nli-model <hf-name-or-path> flag / nli_model= lib
+  param → CITECHECK_NLI_MODEL env var → built-in default. Any HF cross-encoder
+  name or local path; fail fast with clear error if it won't load"
+
+## What you must build (all under /home/hermes/citesure/)
+
+### 1. src/citesure/nli.py
+- Lazy model loading: `get_nli_model(model_name: str | None = None)` —
+  resolves the model name with the D6 priority chain:
+  explicit arg (from --nli-model / nli_model= param) → CITECHECK_NLI_MODEL env
+  → default "cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base".
+  Loads via transformers CrossEncoder (or sentence-transformers if you prefer —
+  your choice, document it). Caches the loaded model in a module-level dict
+  keyed by name so repeated calls don't reload.
+- Cache dir: HF cache should land under ~/.cache/citesure/ (set
+  HF_HOME/HF_HUB_CACHE appropriately when loading, or pass cache_dir=). Make it
+  overridable via env var CITECHECK_CACHE_DIR (consistent with the fetcher).
+- `def score_nli(model, claim: str, passage: str) -> float` — entailment score
+  in [0,1] (softmax over entailment/neutral/contradiction → take entailment
+  probability). Batch-capable: `score_nli_batch(model, pairs) -> list[float]`.
+- CPU-only: force torch device cpu (the venv has torch CPU build). Set
+  torch.set_num_threads sensibly. No GPU assumptions.
+- Fail fast: if the model name/path won't load (bad name, no network for
+  download, corrupt local path), raise a clear error (custom NLIError with an
